              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Scotdog"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delish! I love to make spice mixes homemade. This one is wonderful! I have been using it in my apple cider and also my oatmeal."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "glassycat2330"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe - fresh ground Cardamon (green pods, not black) is a game-changer! It loses flavor rather quickly, though, so store bought is nowhere near as full flavored &amp; addictive as freshly preparing your own. Seriously- the difference will blow your mind! We like to grind fresh green Cardamon seeds in our spice mill or with our cute mortor/pestle, and freeze the excess powder to keep the flavor fresh as we need it.",
            "datePublished": "2025-05-28T21:43:38.426Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rouxanna"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Omg! My house smells amazing. I tweaked the recipe a little. Added half a teaspoon of ginger and half a teaspoon of all spice.... MMM MMM good",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-13T01:44:15.210Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "nzmrsjones"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great to go as is, but it also gave me a starting point to experiment with adding other spices. I have since added allspice, clove and ginger to this mix. I know can get my family to eat oatmeal for breakfast by adding this mix, craisins and nuts to it. I've used the mix in pies, cakes, baked apples, muffins, etc. It's a keeper as is or tweaked to a family's tastes. Thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2011-11-20T05:12:44.330Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SLJ6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious! Could not find cardamom anywhere! So I added 1/2 tsp of allspice and decreased the nutmeg to just 1 tsp. wonderful in Crunchy Apple Pie Granola from this site.",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-09T16:58:28.577Z"
          },
          {
