              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "elcue"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thanks for this, and to the reader who suggested adding ginger and allspice. Mixing your own spice or herb combos is so easy, saves quite a bit of money, avoids unwanted additives, and allows for improved freshness and flavor by mixing smaller batches. I mix Italian, taco, fajita and everything seasoning (and now apple pie seasoning) with ingredients already on hand. Recipes readily available online.",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-09T17:58:32.205Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbi Struble"
            },
            "reviewBody": "just a note of thanks for posting this. I've been using quite a bit of this spice for another recipe..and the price in the grocery store for the very little container seems pretty expensive! I can make this with spices I have on hand. (I was able to purchase ground cardamom pretty cheap and have other uses for it too!) Thanks again!",
            "datePublished": "2006-12-23T10:36:51.213Z"
